{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1rwugmyHdHybVUrPFa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't commit the six weeks yet. Get legal review and run cheap validation first, and narrow the scope.**\n\n**Why not build now**\n- **The evidence is thin.** The tips test raised completion by 3 points (61% → 64%). That shows photo help is worth something, but not that AI selection beats it. We also don't know if that result was statistically significant, or whether completion actually leads to more matches or better retention.\n- **The risk is high.** A dating app asking for someone's whole photo library is a big trust ask. Libraries hold intimate photos, photos of children, documents and other people's faces. Many users may decline the permission, and the request could make some distrust the app. App store rules, GDPR/biometric-data law and how we handle face analysis all need legal review before we design anything, not after.\n- **It's expensive.** About 12 engineer-weeks, based on a guess about demand.\n\n**What to do instead**\n1. **Get legal review now.** It runs in parallel and costs no engineering time.\n2. **Ask fewer permissions.** Use the system photo picker: users choose 10–20 candidates and on-device AI ranks them. This avoids full-library access, likely cuts the build time, and keeps most of the value.\n3. **Test demand cheaply.** Try a fake-door test (\"Let AI pick your best photos\") to measure opt-in, or have staff pick photos by hand for a small group. Do some quick user interviews about how comfortable people feel with this.\n4. **Set go/no-go criteria in advance.** For example: opt-in of at least X%, a completion lift clearly above the tips screen's 3 points, a measurable effect on matches, and legal approval.\n5. **Keep the tips screen live** and treat it as the baseline to beat.\n\nIf those checks pass, build the picker-based version first. Only consider full-library access if the data clearly justifies it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3197,"cache_read_input_tokens":5008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3197},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9138d552-4cdb-41e9-9f11-9d7a44a0fff1","uuid":"d7cf5649-a9ed-4663-a7ec-4fe756ed3dc0","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:17:47.008Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1rwgXnssnpQDdgSL12"}
